# UI-MINIMAP-2: in the continuous zoom the magnifier's - reaches the mouse wheel's furthest
# zoom-out (owner decision 2026-11-17, ui_6.mp4; docs/re/ui.md 2.9). Its stages
# (magnifier_stages): the built levels' tile widths 84, 42, 20, then one halving per press (10,
# 5, 2.5, ...) while wider than the wheel's end, then that end itself (zoom.min_tile: zoom_floor,
# lan5 fitting the 1024 x 768 window, below a pixel). The + walks back through the same stages.
# zoom.target and zoom.min_tile are tile widths in thousandths of a pixel; zoom.at_min is 1 when
# the view's target is the wheel's end. The stepped zoom's clamp: ui_magnifier_range_stepped.
# Launch (--gpu: the continuous zoom needs the GPU renderer): --play data/maps/lan5.txt
# --construction-menu on --layout data/ui
resize 1024 768
wait frames 5
look 1140 516
wait frames 5
expect fact view.tile_w == 20
expect fact zoom.target == 20000
expect fact zoom.at_min == 0
# lan5 at 1024 x 768: the wheel's end lies more than three halvings past level 2, so the first
# three presses below are fixed widths.
expect fact zoom.min_tile < 2500
# The magnifier's - (826, 153), 19 x 21: one halving per press past level 2.
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target == 10000
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target == 5000
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target == 2500
# On until nothing changes: more presses than stages can remain (--max-derived-levels 8 by
# default), a press at the end changes nothing. The view then targets the wheel's end exactly.
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 2
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.at_min == 1
note fact zoom.target
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target same
expect fact zoom.at_min == 1
# The magnifier's + (796, 135): back through the same stages until nothing changes, at level 0.
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
expect fact zoom.at_min == 0
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 2
click_px 805 145
wait frames 3
expect fact view.tile_w == 84
expect fact zoom.target == 84000
click_px 805 145
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target == 84000
# And the - from level 0 down through the built levels into the halvings again.
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target == 42000
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target == 20000
click_px 835 163
wait frames 3
expect fact zoom.target == 10000
expect fact selection.clicks == 0
expect fact camera.pans == 0
quit
